{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01MDbV4G8RR3yhX8yj3EAjyX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specs. Re-implementations diverge on edge cases. This project derives specs from C source, generates Go implementations, and verifies them via differential testing against GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture**: `cmd/` (per-utility binaries), `pkg/testutils/` (differential test harness), `pkg/sys/` (syscall abstractions), `pkg/format/` (output formatting), `magefiles/` (build targets), `docs/` (specifications).\n\n**Implementation state** (from source_code, which takes precedence over prose):\n- `pkg/testutils/`, `pkg/sys/`, `pkg/format/` — all exist with tests\n- `cmd/version/` — exists with tests\n- `cmd/wc/` — exists with main.go + wc_test.go (differential tests)\n- `cmd/cat/` — main.go exists, **cat_test.go is missing**\n- `cmd/sponge/` — no source code\n- `cmd/du/` — no source code\n\n**Current release priority**: rel00.0 and rel01.0 are complete (code exists). rel01.1 (cat) is the earliest incomplete release — implementation exists but differential tests are missing. rel01.2 (sponge) and rel01.3 (du) have no code at all.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nThe earliest gap is **rel01.1**: `cmd/cat/main.go` exists but `cmd/cat/cat_test.go` does not. Differential tests are the gating verification mechanism (ARCHITECTURE DD2). This must be completed before moving to rel01.2 (sponge).\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"prd006-cat R1-R5 -- differential tests for cmd/cat\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - cmd/cat/main.go (implementation under test -- review all flags and error paths)\n      - cmd/wc/wc_test.go (reference pattern for differential test file structure)\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest.go (DiffTest struct, RunDiffTests, NormalizeFunc API)\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd006-cat.yaml (requirements R1-R5 being verified)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-01.1.yaml (test cases to implement as differential tests)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/cat/cat_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Differential tests comparing Go cat binary against GNU gcat reference\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: >\n          Test file concatenation in default mode: stdin when no files given (prd006-cat R1.2),\n          named file argument (prd006-cat R1.1), multiple files concatenated in order\n          (prd006-cat R1.3), and \"-\" argument reading stdin (prd006-cat R4.1). Use\n          testutils.RunDiffTests for all cases.\n      - id: R2\n        text: >\n          Test line numbering flags: -n numbers all output lines (prd006-cat R2.1),\n          -b numbers non-blank lines only (prd006-cat R2.2), and -b overrides -n when\n          both are given (prd006-cat R2.3). Include cases with consecutive blank lines\n          to verify numbering interaction with blank-line squeezing.\n      - id: R3\n        text: >\n          Test display transformation flags: -s squeezes consecutive blank lines\n          (prd006-cat R3.1, R3.2), -E appends $ at end of each line (prd006-cat R4.3),\n          -T displays tabs as ^I (prd006-cat R4.4), -v displays non-printing characters\n          using caret and M- notation (prd006-cat R4.1, R4.2), combination flags -A\n          equivalent to -vET (prd006-cat R4.5), -e equivalent to -vE (prd006-cat R4.6),\n          -t equivalent to -vT (prd006-cat R4.7), and -u accepted but ignored\n          (prd006-cat R4.8).\n      - id: R4\n        text: >\n          Test error handling: missing file prints error to stderr and exits 1\n          (prd006-cat R5.2), mix of valid and invalid files processes valid files\n          and still exits 1 (prd006-cat R5.2). Include an empty-file test to verify\n          zero-byte input produces no output.\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: >\n          Follow the exact structural pattern in cmd/wc/wc_test.go: TestMain function\n          builds the Go binary to a temp directory via go build and locates the GNU\n          reference binary via exec.LookPath. Package-level vars goBinaryPath and\n          refBinaryPath hold the paths. Cleanup removes the temp directory after all\n          tests run.\n      - id: D2\n        text: >\n          The GNU reference binary name is \"gcat\" (GNU cat installed via Homebrew,\n          matching the project convention of g-prefixed binaries per ARCHITECTURE DD4).\n      - id: D3\n        text: >\n          Use a writeFile helper (same as cmd/wc/wc_test.go) to create test fixtures\n          in t.TempDir(). Pass file names relative to WorkDir in DiffTest.Args so both\n          binaries resolve them identically.\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: cmd/cat/cat_test.go compiles with no errors via go build ./cmd/cat/\n      - id: AC2\n        text: >\n          Every test function uses testutils.RunDiffTests with goBinaryPath and\n          refBinaryPath -- no manual expected-output constants\n      - id: AC3\n        text: >\n          Test coverage includes: stdin default, named file, multiple files in order,\n          \"-\" argument, -n, -b, -b overriding -n, -s with consecutive blanks, -E, -T,\n          -v with control chars and high bytes, -A, -e, -t, -u, missing file error,\n          mixed valid/invalid files, and empty file\n      - id: AC4\n        text: go test ./cmd/cat/ passes when gcat is available on PATH\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":61410,"cache_read_input_tokens":19292,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":61410},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"457c6a68-8489-436f-ab4d-95a44750b86c